WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
Two black inks look exactly the same.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.590
Put a dot of each near the
bottom of a strip of paper,

3
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.690
and stand the strip
in a little solvent.

4
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.830
Slowly, the solvent
creeps up the paper.

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.590
One ink splits into
three coloured spots.

6
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.930
The other splits into two.

7
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.190
So how can a strip of
paper pull a mixture apart,

8
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.810
and how can a spot's position
tell you which dye it is?

9
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.030
In this mission, you'll choose
the right way to separate a

10
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:27.580
mixture.

11
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.430
You'll run a chromatogram,

12
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.610
tell a pure substance from a mixture,

13
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.310
and use R-f values to
identify each spot.

14
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.090
Your mission: explain how paper
chromatography separates and

15
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.970
identifies dyes.
